# Real 301 redirects for the retired URLs. Generated by _work/build-redirects.js from the
# canonical tag on each stub page, so the map cannot drift from the pages themselves.
#
# Why. Those URLs return HTTP 200 with a meta refresh, because GitHub Pages cannot issue a redirect,
# and Google treats a meta refresh as a weak hint. Measured on 13 October 2026, /insights-events,
# /opportunities, /database-pro.html and /events.html together took 284 clicks and 7,272 impressions,
# 62% of the site's search impressions, while /data did not appear in the top ten pages at all. The
# authority is stranded on holding pages. Only a 301 consolidates it.
#
# Read by Netlify, and by Vercel through a small config. Inert on GitHub Pages, so it is safe to keep
# here either way. Moving the host is one DNS change: point the www CNAME at the new host. MX, SPF,
# DKIM and DMARC are untouched, so mail cannot be affected, and reverting is the same single record.
#
# from                     to                status
